1
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:06,054
{\an8}SCREAM THE NAME OF THE PERSON YOU LOVE!

2
00:00:07,222 --> 00:00:08,056
[Taiki sighs]

3
00:00:09,266 --> 00:00:10,559
- [Taiki] The person...
- [gasps]

4
00:00:11,226 --> 00:00:13,061
- [Taiki] ...I like is...
- [Hina sighs]

5
00:00:13,145 --> 00:00:14,938
[both] Mm-hm. Mm-hm.

6
00:00:20,152 --> 00:00:21,570
{\an8}It's Yusa, meow!

7
00:00:21,653 --> 00:00:22,779
{\an8}[all] Huh?

8
00:00:23,655 --> 00:00:27,784
{\an8}When he was sleeping on the bus,
he was mumbling about Yusa.

9
00:00:27,868 --> 00:00:29,077
{\an8}"Your smashes are fast!"

10
00:00:29,619 --> 00:00:31,288
{\an8}He likes him so much he dreams about him.

11
00:00:31,371 --> 00:00:32,456
{\an8}Really?

12
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:35,584
So he's in a love triangle
with Moriya, meow.

13
00:00:36,209 --> 00:00:37,127
[gasps]

14
00:00:37,669 --> 00:00:38,670
[Kyo] Hm.

15
00:00:39,421 --> 00:00:41,465
[mischievous music playing]

16
00:00:42,090 --> 00:00:43,675
You're goin' down, Inota!

17
00:00:44,217 --> 00:00:46,261
This fight sounds fiercer
than a badminton match!

18
00:00:46,344 --> 00:00:47,471
I'm not fighting her!

19
00:00:48,138 --> 00:00:50,140
[Nishida] Ayame and Taiki
are about to face off!

20
00:00:50,223 --> 00:00:51,683
[Taiki] What? Like, on the court?

21
00:00:52,309 --> 00:00:54,227
It's late. It's time
you all went to sleep.

22
00:00:54,811 --> 00:00:57,397
{\an8}[Ayame] What? Things were
just getting good, though!

23
00:00:57,481 --> 00:00:58,982
{\an8}[teacher] Wrap it up! Wrap it up.

24
00:01:00,317 --> 00:01:01,651
Goodnight!

25
00:01:05,197 --> 00:01:06,198
Thanks for earlier.

26
00:01:07,074 --> 00:01:10,327
It's not like anyone expected you
to give a real answer, anyway.

27
00:01:10,410 --> 00:01:11,995
Still, though, I appreciate it.

28
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:14,664
But you acknowledge...

29
00:01:16,958 --> 00:01:18,502
that you were hesitating.

30
00:01:18,585 --> 00:01:19,503
[gasps]

31
00:01:29,888 --> 00:01:31,932
[Taiki] <i>It's not that I was hesitating.</i>

32
00:01:33,683 --> 00:01:36,895
<i>I'm in love with Chinatsu.
That hasn't changed.</i>

33
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:39,356
<i>But...</i>

34
00:01:40,774 --> 00:01:42,067
<i>Hina and I...</i>

35
00:01:42,150 --> 00:01:44,569
<i>have had some good moments together
as friends.</i>

36
00:01:44,653 --> 00:01:46,154
REPORT CARDS
STRETCH

37
00:01:46,238 --> 00:01:49,908
<i>And maybe she has made
my heart skip a beat a time or two.</i>

38
00:01:49,991 --> 00:01:53,537
My methodology is to date anybody
who tells me they like me.

39
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:55,664
[Taiki] <i>Now I get what Ayame was saying.</i>

40
00:01:57,958 --> 00:01:59,292
<i>My head is spinning...</i>

41
00:02:02,337 --> 00:02:03,338
[groans]

42
00:02:04,005 --> 00:02:05,674
[slow instrumental music playing]

43
00:02:05,757 --> 00:02:06,925
<i>and spinning.</i>

44
00:02:11,847 --> 00:02:13,849
[opening theme song playing]

45
00:02:38,206 --> 00:02:41,626
BLUE BOX

46
00:03:41,728 --> 00:03:45,941
{\an8}EPISODE 23
SPINNING

47
00:03:46,024 --> 00:03:48,443
[yawns] I'm so tired.

48
00:03:48,526 --> 00:03:50,445
My entire body is sore.

49
00:03:50,528 --> 00:03:52,864
Three more days of this is gonna be...

50
00:03:53,406 --> 00:03:54,449
hell.

51
00:03:56,284 --> 00:03:57,953
Badminton club! Morning!

52
00:03:58,036 --> 00:04:00,705
Let's get out there and carpe that diem!

53
00:04:00,789 --> 00:04:02,374
How's this dude so hyped up?

54
00:04:02,457 --> 00:04:03,833
Must be a morning person.

55
00:04:05,585 --> 00:04:08,088
[Taiki] <i>I gotta get ready
to focus on practice.</i>

56
00:04:08,171 --> 00:04:11,508
<i>If I let the other stuff get in my head,
this will all be for nothing.</i>

57
00:04:11,591 --> 00:04:12,467
[boy] Hey.

58
00:04:14,678 --> 00:04:17,347
Somebody left this tote bag behind
in the lobby.

59
00:04:17,430 --> 00:04:18,473
Whose is it?

60
00:04:21,851 --> 00:04:25,355
It's Hina's.
She's my friend from gymnastics.

61
00:04:26,189 --> 00:04:28,483
- I can get it to her.
- You sure?

62
00:04:29,359 --> 00:04:32,237
'Cause the gymnastics bus
is heading out it looks like.

63
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:33,905
[gasps] What?

64
00:04:35,865 --> 00:04:37,701
[Taiki] Hey! Stop the bus!

65
00:04:37,784 --> 00:04:39,995
- Stop the bus!
- [Hina exclaims softly]

66
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:44,374
[pants]

67
00:04:46,126 --> 00:04:48,211
I'm already out of gas this early?

68
00:04:49,212 --> 00:04:51,006
Here, Hina. You left this behind.

69
00:04:53,466 --> 00:04:54,509
Thanks, Taiki.

70
00:04:57,429 --> 00:04:58,346
See ya!

71
00:05:12,694 --> 00:05:14,446
[inspirational music playing]

72
00:05:17,991 --> 00:05:19,909
[grunting]

73
00:05:20,869 --> 00:05:21,911
Ten more seconds!

74
00:05:22,537 --> 00:05:24,205
[grunts, pants]

75
00:05:28,043 --> 00:05:30,086
[Taiki thuds, racket clatters]

76
00:05:38,011 --> 00:05:39,179
[Nishida] Eat up, lads!

77
00:05:39,262 --> 00:05:42,432
Eat up! Eating is part of training,
you know! [munches loudly]

78
00:05:43,016 --> 00:05:45,727
Eat some of those pickles!
And those shallots, too!

79
00:05:45,810 --> 00:05:47,729
You should have vegetables, too, Nishida--

80
00:05:47,812 --> 00:05:49,314
Don't take my katsu!

81
00:05:49,397 --> 00:05:52,817
[sighs] Could you please be more mindful
of your table manners, guys?

82
00:05:52,901 --> 00:05:54,444
What are you talking about?

83
00:05:54,527 --> 00:05:56,654
During mealtime, we're at war!

84
00:05:56,738 --> 00:05:59,324
The basketball club
doesn't seem to think so.

85
00:05:59,407 --> 00:06:02,702
Hm. Nothing hits the spot
like Japanese rice.

86
00:06:02,786 --> 00:06:04,996
Like, in the U.S., all they eat is steak.

87
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:09,125
{\an8}- The vibe is different over there.
- I am not a fan of that handsome laddie.

88
00:06:09,209 --> 00:06:11,544
{\an8}So you admit that he is handsome, then?

89
00:06:11,628 --> 00:06:15,381
{\an8}There exist, in this world,
certain facts that cannot be denied.

90
00:06:15,465 --> 00:06:17,092
[groans] Too much!

91
00:06:17,926 --> 00:06:20,678
I like him, actually. Matsuoka.

92
00:06:22,472 --> 00:06:24,265
{\an8}He hooks me up with great gear.

93
00:06:24,349 --> 00:06:25,600
{\an8}You game together?

94
00:06:25,683 --> 00:06:27,602
My sister's talked to you about that.

95
00:06:28,228 --> 00:06:30,021
He's good at basketball,

96
00:06:30,105 --> 00:06:32,607
he stays in shape,
and I respect him for that.

97
00:06:32,690 --> 00:06:33,942
Mm-hm. Mm-hm.

98
00:06:35,193 --> 00:06:36,945
They'd be a perfect couple.

99
00:06:37,529 --> 00:06:38,613
[Nishida] Who would?

100
00:06:40,615 --> 00:06:42,617
[inspirational music ends]

101
00:06:46,704 --> 00:06:48,456
I'll get a change of clothes.

102
00:06:48,540 --> 00:06:49,582
Okay, dude.

103
00:06:55,255 --> 00:06:56,256
Oh.

104
00:06:56,339 --> 00:06:57,423
GUEST ROOM

105
00:06:57,507 --> 00:06:59,050
Hi, Chinatsu.

106
00:06:59,134 --> 00:07:00,802
Hi, Taiki. How's it--

107
00:07:00,885 --> 00:07:01,719
Huh?

108
00:07:02,429 --> 00:07:04,597
- Hey.
- Huh? Yes?

109
00:07:05,849 --> 00:07:08,268
<i>She hasn't grabbed my shirt in a while.</i>

110
00:07:09,060 --> 00:07:10,895
What did you do to your elbow?

111
00:07:12,105 --> 00:07:13,523
What?

112
00:07:13,606 --> 00:07:15,024
Oh, that...

113
00:07:15,108 --> 00:07:16,025
SKID

114
00:07:16,109 --> 00:07:17,527
I took a spill earlier!

115
00:07:17,610 --> 00:07:20,280
Well, you can't go around
without a bandage on.

116
00:07:21,114 --> 00:07:23,032
[Taiki] <i>I need a bandage?</i>

117
00:07:23,116 --> 00:07:24,284
This is nothing.

118
00:07:24,868 --> 00:07:26,369
Uh... hang on a sec.

119
00:07:27,871 --> 00:07:29,289
[playful music playing]

120
00:07:29,873 --> 00:07:32,292
Do you always carry bandages with you?

121
00:07:32,375 --> 00:07:34,878
I kinda get hurt all the time, so...

122
00:07:35,879 --> 00:07:37,547
[bandage crinkling]

123
00:07:40,133 --> 00:07:42,302
- Now the art!
- A pen?

124
00:07:43,094 --> 00:07:45,597
- [Taiki] Ah, that tickles!
- [Chinatsu] Stop moving!

125
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:46,556
[pen scratching]

126
00:07:48,141 --> 00:07:49,058
There!

127
00:07:51,144 --> 00:07:54,063
{\an8}- Water bottle?
- No, it's a boar, silly!

128
00:07:54,939 --> 00:07:55,815
[Nagisa] Huh?

129
00:07:56,483 --> 00:07:57,567
Where's Natsu?

130
00:07:58,359 --> 00:08:00,111
I guess I should get going.

131
00:08:01,362 --> 00:08:02,322
See ya!

132
00:08:09,954 --> 00:08:11,581
[inaudible]

133
00:08:13,416 --> 00:08:14,584
[exclaims softly]

134
00:08:18,755 --> 00:08:20,089
[playful music ends]

135
00:08:20,173 --> 00:08:23,092
{\an8}UEDA SHIKI HOTEL
YACHO FOREST - OBSERVATION DECK

136
00:08:27,013 --> 00:08:27,847
Huh?

137
00:08:27,931 --> 00:08:29,891
Yo, yo, yo, yo.

138
00:08:29,974 --> 00:08:31,392
How's it going?

139
00:08:31,476 --> 00:08:32,685
What's up?

140
00:08:32,769 --> 00:08:34,354
I don't see Chinatsu...

141
00:08:34,979 --> 00:08:36,898
That would be because she went on a run.

142
00:08:36,981 --> 00:08:39,609
She said something crazy
like she hadn't trained enough today.

143
00:08:40,318 --> 00:08:41,861
Did she go out by herself?

144
00:08:41,945 --> 00:08:44,864
[Nagisa] Yeah, she said
she'd stay close by, so it's fine.

145
00:08:44,948 --> 00:08:47,909
We just don't have
the stamina to keep up with her.

146
00:08:47,992 --> 00:08:50,620
She's got demonic energy levels.

147
00:08:51,579 --> 00:08:52,664
Okay, got it.

148
00:08:55,333 --> 00:08:56,251
You a fan of hers?

149
00:08:58,253 --> 00:08:59,254
[Taiki internally] <i>"Fan"?</i>

150
00:08:59,879 --> 00:09:02,131
First-year badminton player, right?

151
00:09:02,215 --> 00:09:04,717
Natsu's passionate about her training.

152
00:09:04,801 --> 00:09:06,511
She's always been that way.

153
00:09:06,594 --> 00:09:09,556
[Taiki] <i>Yeah, I know that.
And why are you acting like her boyfriend?</i>

154
00:09:09,639 --> 00:09:11,432
Why're you acting like her boyfriend?

155
00:09:11,516 --> 00:09:13,142
[Taiki] <i>Nagisa!</i>

156
00:09:13,226 --> 00:09:14,978
Huh? Am I?

157
00:09:15,562 --> 00:09:16,521
[Nagisa sighs]

158
00:09:16,604 --> 00:09:17,897
Come on, let's get going.

159
00:09:17,981 --> 00:09:20,149
[Taiki groans internally]

160
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:23,903
<i>I am 100% not about this guy.</i>

161
00:09:24,487 --> 00:09:27,699
Our Natsu is just as popular
as ever, isn't she?

162
00:09:27,782 --> 00:09:30,034
Well, people would wait
for her after games.

163
00:09:30,118 --> 00:09:31,911
Oh, yeah. I totally remember that.

164
00:09:32,537 --> 00:09:35,331
[Kazuma] There was an upperclassman
I admired like that, too.

165
00:09:37,542 --> 00:09:40,044
<i>Could you not lump me in
with the two of you?</i>

166
00:09:40,128 --> 00:09:42,922
<i>Chinatsu and I are living together!</i>

167
00:09:43,923 --> 00:09:45,967
<i>He used the word "admired."</i>

168
00:09:47,135 --> 00:09:51,472
<i>It's almost like he's saying
what I feel for Chinatsu isn't love.</i>

169
00:10:01,024 --> 00:10:02,984
[footsteps receding]

170
00:10:08,573 --> 00:10:10,241
- [boys laughing]
- What's up with that?

171
00:10:10,325 --> 00:10:12,243
That's what I'm saying, bro.
It's a mystery.

172
00:10:12,327 --> 00:10:14,579
- Dude, no way.
- Makes no sense. Am I right?

173
00:10:15,204 --> 00:10:16,497
Dude, I reek of sweat!

174
00:10:16,581 --> 00:10:18,166
- Man, it's so hot.
- Hoo!

175
00:10:21,336 --> 00:10:23,379
- Um...
- [chuckling]

176
00:10:23,463 --> 00:10:24,547
- [all] Huh?
- Hm?

177
00:10:25,089 --> 00:10:27,008
Hey, have you seen Taiki?

178
00:10:27,717 --> 00:10:28,801
Huh?

179
00:10:28,885 --> 00:10:31,304
When was the last time we saw him, anyway?

180
00:10:31,387 --> 00:10:34,307
He was at the evening session. I think.

181
00:10:34,390 --> 00:10:35,266
[Kyo grunts]

182
00:10:35,933 --> 00:10:37,602
[boy] Maybe he's in the bath.

183
00:10:37,685 --> 00:10:38,770
Oh, got it.

184
00:10:42,857 --> 00:10:44,442
[footsteps running]

185
00:10:44,525 --> 00:10:45,777
UEDA SHIKI HOTEL

186
00:10:45,860 --> 00:10:48,905
[Taiki] <i>I'm genuinely worried
about her running alone at night.</i>

187
00:10:48,988 --> 00:10:51,783
<i>And, coincidentally,
I wanted to go on a run myself.</i>

188
00:10:51,866 --> 00:10:55,036
<i>I am absolutely not,
in any way, stalking Chinatsu!</i>

189
00:10:59,082 --> 00:11:02,710
<i>If it were Hina,
I would've done the same thing.</i>

190
00:11:03,628 --> 00:11:05,046
[wind blowing]

191
00:11:05,129 --> 00:11:06,506
[mellow music playing]

192
00:11:07,423 --> 00:11:11,803
<i>I know that there are a lot of things
I need to spend some time thinking about.</i>

193
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:16,724
[chuckles softly]

194
00:11:17,642 --> 00:11:20,103
<i>But the more I think about them,</i>

195
00:11:20,186 --> 00:11:22,313
<i>the less sure I am
that those thoughts are my own.</i>

196
00:11:24,399 --> 00:11:26,109
{\an8}But I feel like you might've added

197
00:11:26,192 --> 00:11:29,570
{\an8}an extra 30% or so
of feelings for Hina, you know?

198
00:11:31,114 --> 00:11:34,075
[Taiki] <i>Like water
after you've washed a brush in it.</i>

199
00:11:35,159 --> 00:11:38,579
My methodology is to date anybody
who tells me they like me.

200
00:11:39,205 --> 00:11:42,583
[Taiki] <i>Or like mixing together
different drinks at a soda fountain.</i>

201
00:11:45,378 --> 00:11:48,047
[Kazuma] <i>There was an upperclassman
I admired like that, too.</i>

202
00:11:49,173 --> 00:11:53,594
[Taiki] <i>But I think that loving someone
should be more intuitive, right?</i>

203
00:11:54,429 --> 00:11:56,431
<i>And on the topic of my feelings...</i>

204
00:11:59,475 --> 00:12:03,980
<i>I'm pretty sure that
I'm starting to see Hina as a girl.</i>

205
00:12:11,904 --> 00:12:13,030
[Hina] <i>I like you.</i>

206
00:12:13,865 --> 00:12:15,658
[Taiki] <i>After she said that...</i>

207
00:12:15,741 --> 00:12:19,537
That's fine, as long as it reminds you
that I have a crush on you.

208
00:12:20,663 --> 00:12:23,875
<i>It'd be nice to see the guy I like
doing his best.</i>

209
00:12:23,958 --> 00:12:25,042
[Taiki] <i>Little by little.</i>

210
00:12:26,711 --> 00:12:28,004
[inaudible]

211
00:12:38,181 --> 00:12:40,349
[Taiki] <i>And so, the more time passes,</i>

212
00:12:40,433 --> 00:12:43,102
<i>the harder I'm finding it
to answer her confession.</i>

213
00:12:43,186 --> 00:12:44,061
[mellow music ends]

214
00:12:44,145 --> 00:12:45,813
[pants]

215
00:12:47,982 --> 00:12:49,567
BEWARE OF BEARS

216
00:12:49,650 --> 00:12:51,569
[whimpering]

217
00:12:51,652 --> 00:12:53,571
[epic music playing]

218
00:12:54,655 --> 00:12:56,574
[bear charging]

219
00:12:58,159 --> 00:13:00,286
- [roaring]
- [Chinatsu screams]

220
00:13:00,369 --> 00:13:01,787
[epic music ends]

221
00:13:01,871 --> 00:13:03,498
[breath trembling]

222
00:13:04,832 --> 00:13:05,917
[grunts]

223
00:13:06,918 --> 00:13:10,630
[Taiki] <i>Is it true that I feel
some admiration toward Chinatsu?</i>

224
00:13:10,713 --> 00:13:11,797
<i>Sure.</i>

225
00:13:16,928 --> 00:13:18,554
<i>She's a year older than me.</i>

226
00:13:19,305 --> 00:13:21,557
<i>She's beautiful, and popular.</i>

227
00:13:22,642 --> 00:13:24,018
<i>She works hard.</i>

228
00:13:24,810 --> 00:13:26,479
<i>And she's her own person.</i>

229
00:13:27,104 --> 00:13:29,815
<i>Why would she go out running by herself?</i>

230
00:13:30,858 --> 00:13:32,318
[inaudible]

231
00:13:32,401 --> 00:13:34,779
<i>Yes, the two of us have gotten closer...</i>

232
00:13:35,863 --> 00:13:39,659
<i>but as to what's going on in her head,
I still have no idea.</i>

233
00:13:41,202 --> 00:13:43,037
<i>The fact that I do admire her</i>

234
00:13:43,120 --> 00:13:45,790
<i>is making me realize
there's probably still...</i>

235
00:13:47,041 --> 00:13:48,709
<i>some distance between us.</i>

236
00:13:49,460 --> 00:13:50,503
<i>But...</i>

237
00:13:51,420 --> 00:13:52,505
<i>but still...</i>

238
00:13:56,592 --> 00:14:00,471
<i>It's because I admire her
that I want to be with her.</i>

239
00:14:02,848 --> 00:14:04,058
[Chinatsu] Taiki?

240
00:14:04,684 --> 00:14:05,560
[exclaims]

241
00:14:10,648 --> 00:14:11,941
[gasps]

242
00:14:13,317 --> 00:14:14,694
[Chinatsu gasps]

243
00:14:17,488 --> 00:14:19,448
What is going on here?

244
00:14:19,532 --> 00:14:20,575
I was just...

245
00:14:21,158 --> 00:14:22,952
Here's what's going on!

246
00:14:23,035 --> 00:14:25,246
I went into the mountains
to pick vegetables,

247
00:14:25,329 --> 00:14:27,582
and wouldn't you know it, I hurt my ankle!

248
00:14:27,665 --> 00:14:31,377
But then not long after,
this young lady happened to pass by,

249
00:14:31,460 --> 00:14:33,671
and she's graciously carried me this far.

250
00:14:33,754 --> 00:14:36,048
[exclaims softly]

251
00:14:37,174 --> 00:14:39,719
- Well, let me take over.
- Thanks, Taiki.

252
00:14:40,469 --> 00:14:43,139
Luckily, we came across a payphone
while we were walking,

253
00:14:43,222 --> 00:14:45,600
so I called the hotel
and let them know what happened.

254
00:14:46,183 --> 00:14:48,394
Oh, that was probably after I left.

255
00:14:49,061 --> 00:14:51,522
I do feel quite guilty...

256
00:14:51,606 --> 00:14:54,233
causing all this trouble
for you young people.

257
00:14:54,317 --> 00:14:55,693
I'll carry your basket.

258
00:14:56,861 --> 00:14:59,113
- Aren't you tuckered out?
- [Chinatsu] Not at all!

259
00:14:59,947 --> 00:15:02,116
{\an8}I do exercise every day.

260
00:15:02,199 --> 00:15:03,868
[wind blowing]

261
00:15:04,744 --> 00:15:06,954
[inaudible]

262
00:15:07,038 --> 00:15:09,123
[slow instrumental music playing]

263
00:15:27,475 --> 00:15:28,935
[Taiki] Shall we?

264
00:15:29,018 --> 00:15:30,394
Thanks again.

265
00:15:31,270 --> 00:15:33,397
[Taiki] <i>My favorite color is blue.</i>

266
00:15:34,357 --> 00:15:36,317
<i>My favorite drink is Cola.</i>

267
00:15:38,778 --> 00:15:40,279
<i>That is what I know.</i>

268
00:15:40,363 --> 00:15:42,114
[slow instrumental music ends]

269
00:15:44,533 --> 00:15:46,911
[old woman]
I just can't thank you kids enough.

270
00:15:46,994 --> 00:15:48,913
To sprain my ankle like that,

271
00:15:48,996 --> 00:15:51,916
looks like my age
has finally caught up with me.

272
00:15:51,999 --> 00:15:54,001
Oh, no, that doesn't sound true.

273
00:15:54,085 --> 00:15:57,004
This is what you get
for going into the mountains at night.

274
00:15:57,088 --> 00:15:59,674
I was searching high and low for you,
you know that?

275
00:15:59,757 --> 00:16:01,509
Then I see this young man carrying you.

276
00:16:01,592 --> 00:16:03,552
Good gracious, you're a pain in the neck.

277
00:16:03,636 --> 00:16:05,429
All right, now, Pa, you can it!

278
00:16:05,513 --> 00:16:08,557
Young lady, would you care
for some snacks to take with you?

279
00:16:08,641 --> 00:16:11,143
These are my favorite. They're quite good.

280
00:16:11,227 --> 00:16:12,436
[Chinatsu] Oh, I couldn't.

281
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:15,272
[old man] Surely we have
something better than those!

282
00:16:16,607 --> 00:16:19,527
[old woman] Right! There is the offering
we got for the Buddhist altar--

283
00:16:19,610 --> 00:16:21,445
Oh, I'll gladly take these!

284
00:16:21,529 --> 00:16:22,863
RICE CRACKERS

285
00:16:25,866 --> 00:16:28,202
[old woman] Your boyfriend
deserves my thanks, too.

286
00:16:29,286 --> 00:16:30,413
[Taiki] Boy--

287
00:16:31,580 --> 00:16:34,208
Oh, no! I'm not her boyfriend!

288
00:16:34,834 --> 00:16:37,294
<i>Aw, man! I got all flustered at that.</i>

289
00:16:37,378 --> 00:16:40,006
<i>Now she's bound to get suspicious.</i>

290
00:16:40,089 --> 00:16:42,967
<i>Should I not have denied it
as hard as I just did?</i>

291
00:16:43,551 --> 00:16:44,969
Then again...

292
00:16:45,052 --> 00:16:46,387
[old woman] <i>Is that right?</i>

293
00:16:46,470 --> 00:16:49,598
<i>I was sure that you'd gotten worried
when she didn't come back,</i>

294
00:16:49,682 --> 00:16:52,101
<i>and so you'd gone out looking for her.</i>

295
00:16:52,935 --> 00:16:54,145
[exclaims softly]

296
00:16:55,187 --> 00:16:56,605
[Taiki groans]

297
00:16:56,689 --> 00:16:59,734
Oh, that? Well...
That was only a coincidence!

298
00:16:59,817 --> 00:17:01,944
I was out running and then saw you two.

299
00:17:02,653 --> 00:17:05,614
<i>About 20% of that is true anyway.</i>

300
00:17:05,698 --> 00:17:07,366
All right, young ones.

301
00:17:07,450 --> 00:17:09,493
I'll drive you back to your hotel.

302
00:17:09,577 --> 00:17:11,037
Good idea, hon.

303
00:17:11,120 --> 00:17:13,372
Oh, no! We don't mind walking.

304
00:17:13,456 --> 00:17:15,791
[old man] It's okay.
Let me do this for you.

305
00:17:15,875 --> 00:17:18,878
Plus, I can't have you walk back
when it's pitch black.

306
00:17:23,424 --> 00:17:25,593
[old man] It's the hotel
up in the mountains, right?

307
00:17:25,676 --> 00:17:28,012
[Taiki] Yes. Ueda Shiki Hotel.

308
00:17:28,095 --> 00:17:29,638
[old man] Yep, you betcha.

309
00:17:30,222 --> 00:17:32,516
Honestly, thank you for your help today.

310
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:34,894
Ma is always pushing herself to the limit.

311
00:17:34,977 --> 00:17:37,396
Of course. Do take care of yourselves.

312
00:17:38,022 --> 00:17:39,315
[old man] Why, just last month,

313
00:17:39,398 --> 00:17:42,902
no sooner did I tell her to stay home,
she was already out the door.

314
00:17:42,985 --> 00:17:45,029
[peaceful music playing]

315
00:18:01,045 --> 00:18:02,671
[Taiki] <i>Her profile is just...</i>

316
00:18:13,766 --> 00:18:16,685
WELCOME TO THE UEDA SHIKI HOTEL
THANK YOU FOR STAYING WITH US

317
00:18:19,772 --> 00:18:22,233
The both of you
should get straight to bed.

318
00:18:22,316 --> 00:18:23,442
Yes, sir!

319
00:18:24,777 --> 00:18:25,694
Good night!

320
00:18:27,029 --> 00:18:28,197
Good night. Sleep well.

321
00:18:42,837 --> 00:18:44,964
- [door opens]
- Huh?

322
00:18:45,047 --> 00:18:46,340
You've been gone a while.

323
00:18:49,510 --> 00:18:51,345
[Taiki groans]

324
00:18:52,555 --> 00:18:55,641
[Kyo] <i>I see what's going on.
He went after Chinatsu.</i>

325
00:18:56,934 --> 00:18:58,853
<i>And something definitely happened.</i>

326
00:19:02,439 --> 00:19:05,067
[shuttlecock thudding]

327
00:19:13,492 --> 00:19:15,870
Wow! That was a great play!

328
00:19:15,953 --> 00:19:17,413
Come on, Manager!

329
00:19:17,496 --> 00:19:19,707
It isn't fair if you're playing favorites!

330
00:19:19,790 --> 00:19:22,126
[Ayame] But what he just did
was so impressive!

331
00:19:22,209 --> 00:19:24,211
His attack was totally on point.

332
00:19:24,295 --> 00:19:25,629
[boy] Actually, it was a smash.

333
00:19:26,213 --> 00:19:28,090
[Ayame] And on top of that, Muraoka,

334
00:19:28,174 --> 00:19:30,634
you couldn't return
a shot like that before.

335
00:19:31,594 --> 00:19:33,637
You've grown so much as a player!

336
00:19:34,930 --> 00:19:36,015
Manager...

337
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:38,642
- [Ayame] Keep it up!
- [grunts]

338
00:19:39,476 --> 00:19:40,769
Watch out for that one.

339
00:19:40,853 --> 00:19:42,771
It doesn't mean she's got a crush.

340
00:19:42,855 --> 00:19:44,148
Don't let her fool you.

341
00:19:44,231 --> 00:19:45,649
A real trickster.

342
00:19:46,609 --> 00:19:48,944
The manager is fitting in pretty well.

343
00:19:49,028 --> 00:19:51,363
If that's what you call "fitting in well"!

344
00:19:51,447 --> 00:19:53,949
[Kyo] Trust me,
Muraoka's not taking it to heart.

345
00:19:54,033 --> 00:19:55,534
I mean, I hope you're right.

346
00:20:06,754 --> 00:20:07,796
[Ayame] Hm.

347
00:20:09,006 --> 00:20:11,467
<i>Inota has the best form on the team.</i>

348
00:20:13,385 --> 00:20:16,555
<i>But Yusa's is still better than his.</i>

349
00:20:17,431 --> 00:20:19,391
Oh! They're still practicing.

350
00:20:20,142 --> 00:20:21,518
Hello there.

351
00:20:21,602 --> 00:20:23,020
Rhythmic gymnastics!

352
00:20:23,646 --> 00:20:24,855
Done for today?

353
00:20:24,939 --> 00:20:27,483
We only have weight training left,
so we came back.

354
00:20:27,566 --> 00:20:29,318
And we wanted to pop our heads in.

355
00:20:30,110 --> 00:20:32,196
Hina didn't forget anything?

356
00:20:32,279 --> 00:20:33,822
[Hina] I can hear you!

357
00:20:34,490 --> 00:20:35,574
Oopsie! [chuckles]

358
00:20:35,658 --> 00:20:36,617
Hm.

359
00:20:39,286 --> 00:20:41,830
- We should get a move on.
- Totally.

360
00:20:42,915 --> 00:20:44,500
Good luck with your practice.

361
00:20:44,583 --> 00:20:45,834
[Ayame] Thanksies.

362
00:20:48,254 --> 00:20:49,838
So that worked out.

363
00:20:49,922 --> 00:20:50,839
What did?

364
00:20:50,923 --> 00:20:52,758
You got to see Inomata.

365
00:20:52,841 --> 00:20:54,093
What?

366
00:20:54,176 --> 00:20:57,846
And plus, we see each other all the time.
It's not like I was glad to see him.

367
00:20:57,930 --> 00:21:01,892
[Niina] <i>Right, even when you were looking
all over for him at the hotel.</i>

368
00:21:01,976 --> 00:21:04,853
<i>Honestly, after what happened
at the Cultural Festival,</i>

369
00:21:04,937 --> 00:21:06,814
<i>I really thought they'd get together.</i>

370
00:21:08,607 --> 00:21:11,652
Oh, yeah. Have you heard
about the campfire superstition?

371
00:21:11,735 --> 00:21:14,238
[Hina] That if you confess
to your crush, you'll fall in love?

372
00:21:14,321 --> 00:21:16,699
I know it sounds kinda sketchy.

373
00:21:16,782 --> 00:21:17,866
Yeah, sketchy.

374
00:21:19,243 --> 00:21:21,620
But we're here anyway,
so why don't you try it?

375
00:21:22,288 --> 00:21:24,581
Maybe you'll finally
get an answer from him.

376
00:21:25,874 --> 00:21:26,917
[sighs]

377
00:21:27,459 --> 00:21:29,378
[mellow music playing]

378
00:21:32,006 --> 00:21:33,382
[inaudible]

379
00:21:45,728 --> 00:21:46,812
I won't.

380
00:21:54,445 --> 00:21:57,197
Until Taiki actually
falls in love with me...

381
00:21:57,865 --> 00:21:59,325
I don't need an answer.

382
00:22:00,743 --> 00:22:02,578
[wind blowing]

383
00:22:02,661 --> 00:22:03,662
[mellow music ends]

384
00:22:05,539 --> 00:22:07,541
[closing theme song playing]
